          <change when="2014-12-07T08:51:35.656-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">In lines 21 and 22 the papyrus clearly has "bene baleas" (l. "bene valeas") in Latin characters (Taf. III).  This was recognized by Wilcken, see Chrest.Wilck. 470 and APF 6 (1922), 441, but somehow the reading "bene valeas," BL 1.310 and P.Muench. 1.2, p. 19, has stuck around.  The Greek βενε βαλεας of the ed. pr. need not be retained in the app.</change>
